This packaging targets Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute), whose golang-go package is
Go 1.26. Build a package from a checkout with:

    sudo apt install debhelper golang-go
    dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b

The build needs network access to download the Go modules, or a vendor/
directory made with `go mod vendor`. `DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS=nocheck` skips the
tests.

After installing, initialise or enrol the node once by hand (see
/usr/share/doc/cheesecloth/README.md), put its settings in
/etc/cheesecloth/config.yaml, then `systemctl enable --now cheesecloth`.
